  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Potential for patchy frost tonight and Monday \nnight across the north.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION...\nHigh pressure system has settled over Quebec today. Confidence\nin frost potential is relatively low, since temperatures are\nheavily going to depend on how fast cloud deck moves in. Upper \nair model soundings indicate the weak winds at the surface with \nlower surface dewpoints. Thus, lower RH values which should keep\nfrost potential low. Best chances for patchy frost will be in\nthe North Woods, and Central/Southern Aroostook.\n\nHigh pressure will build toward the region Monday night, with \nclearing skies and decreasing winds. This will create favorable\nconditions for radiational cooling. Patchy/areas of frost are \npossible across northern areas later Monday night, with the \nbetter chances in the normally colder low lying areas.",
